# Repo-wide defaults. This is the fix for the CRLF problem.
#
# Without this file, git stores whatever line endings the committing machine
# used. Windows commits CRLF, and then every file has a ^M at the end of each
# line, diffs are noisy, and a shell script or a Docker context breaks in ways
# that are hard to trace back to line endings.
#
# text=auto: git normalises to LF in the repository and converts back to the
# platform's endings on checkout. That is what you want for source code.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-only files must keep CRLF, or cmd.exe will not run them.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Never touch line endings in binaries - the conversion corrupts them.
*.pdf binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
